HTML rules for usage tags:
1. Use <header> for:
   - Site title.
   - Logo.
   - Navigation.
2. Use <section> for:
   - A stand-alone section of content.
3. Use <footer> for:
   - Copyright information.
   - Terms and Conditions.
4. Use <main> for:
   - The main content of the document.
   - Unique content that is not repeated across pages.
   - Should only appear once per page.